		{"id":"ac7d37827f91a411","type":"file","file":"4 - Senior Year/Fall 2025/Ancient Philosophy/!Papers/Paper 1 - Parmenides/Fragment Notes/Parmenides Fragment 20.md","x":-1960,"y":-883,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"834240ed7fd7ed70","type":"file","file":"General Notes/Ancient Philosophy - Week 2 Day 1 2025-09-02 10.29.34.excalidraw.png","x":-1560,"y":-186,"width":680,"height":490},
		{"id":"52bd109f6a636281","type":"text","text":"# Science\n- **Fragment 2**: Something is when it is able to be *investigated* and illustrates *Truth*\n- **Fragment 6**: Even in Science, there is not an existence of *nothing*. Even in the most desolate parts of space, we now know that \n- **Fragment 7**: The sense of reality is able to be captured by Logic\n\t- Unmoving: Science and it’s fundamental rules are unmovable\n\t- Ungenerable: Constants in math and science have been discovered and are true *throughout* the universe\n\t- Indestructible: Even if humans did not exist, science and it’s laws would exist\n- **Fragment 8**: \n\t- From an atomic standpoint, the fundamental particles of the universe do not change in Parmenides sense.\n\t\t- Leaf changing from fall from green to red does not imply a change from nothing to something, as the leaf has the *same composition* of materials inside of it\n\t- “Our scientific understanding of the world of appearance is only a mortal opinion and is *not* knowledge; for the world of appearance is not an object of knowledge.”","x":-2720,"y":-1160,"width":537,"height":499},
		{"id":"1847b671bf5e0a36","type":"text","text":"# Sense of Is\n- **Fragment 2**: Truth is based around the difference of “what is\" and “what is not”\n- **Fragment 3**: A sense of “Is” comes from being able to *noein* about it. Thinking and being *should be the same*\n- **Fragment 6**: Nothing does not exist since it cannot be thought of. Since thinking and being are the same, nothing can exist\n- **Fragment 7**: The *world of appearance* is a combination of “is” and “not is”, which means it is deceptive and illusory. We must *noein* with our *NOUS* to grasp beyond the “what is not”\n- **Fragment 8**: Something that “is\" cannot change since motion implies a transition from “what-is” to “what-is-not”\n- **Fragment 20**: to be is, it has to be unmoving and singular and not a combination","x":-2460,"y":-186,"width":500,"height":358}
	],
